  ('AMR110B-030', 'LIVE Electrical AMR110B-030 Single Module 10A B Curve 30mA Type A Bidirectional Mini RCBO', 'live-double-pole-bidirectional-rcbo-mini-b-curve-10amp-30ma', 'AMR is a range of MCB sized RCBOs, apply to circuit of AC50/60Hz. Rated voltage to 230V, and current up to 40 A, bring higher levels of safety to an electrical installation and its users because they include switched neutral as standard, which will guarantee that healthy circuits remain in service and that only a faulty circuit is switched off and bring cost savings by reducing installation and testing times. Specifications: Rated voltage (Ue): 230V AC Breaking capacity (Icn): 6kA Rated residual current: 30mA, 100mA Tripping characteristic: B, C Electrical endurance: 4000 cycles Mechanical endurance: 100000 cycles Complies with BS EN 61009-1 Type: AC, A Switching and isolation Overload and short circuit protection. Protection against the effects of sinusoidal alternation earth fault currents Indirect and direct contacts protection Protection against fire hazard caused by insulation fa…', 'Live Electrical', '{}'::jsonb, '/images/products/AMRImage.jpg', 'disjoncteurs-differentiels-rcbo'),
  ('AFDD064030B', 'Fusebox Arc Fault Detection Device RCBO 30mA AFDD 40Amp', 'fusebox-arc-fault-detection-device-rcbo-30ma-afdd-40amp', 'FuseBox’s AFDD is a single module device which is suitable for new and existing FuseBox installations. Designed to protect against ARC FAULTS (Series and Parallel), overload, short circuit and earth leakage. The AFDD06 is double pole RCBO AFDD meaning the Line and Neutral conductors do not have to be disconnected for IR (insulation resistance) testing if the lever is in the OFF position making it the ideal solution any property requiring AFDD protection. Arc fault protection devices (AFDD) are designed to help prevent fires by identifying fire propagating electrical arcs. These can be caused by a number of things such as rodent damage, faulty cable insulation, crushed wires or even loose terminals. These devices combine conventional analogue measurements with microprocessors to quickly analyse data. The quick ‘decision making’ of the unit allows it to detect potential faults before th…', 'Fusebox', '{"Caractéristique 1":"Available in 6A, 10A, 16A, 20A, 32A, 40A","Caractéristique 2":"Retrofit to any FuseBox Consumer Unit","Caractéristique 3":"Single module","Caractéristique 4":"Double Pole RCBO 1P+N (switched)","Caractéristique 5":"Type A for AC and pulsating DC sensitivity","Caractéristique 6":"Short circuit capacity of 6kA with a maximum rating of 40A","Caractéristique 7":"LED indication","Caractéristique 8":"Fully compliant and 3rd party tested to BS EN 62606 / IEC 61009-1"}'::jsonb, '/images/products/AFDD06faultdetectiondevice30mA.png', 'detecteurs-arc-afdd'),
  ('AFDD061030B', 'Fusebox Arc Fault Detection Device RCBO 30mA AFDD 10Amp', 'fusebox-arc-fault-detection-device-rcbo-30ma-afdd-10amp', 'FuseBox’s AFDD is a single module device which is suitable for new and existing FuseBox installations. Designed to protect against ARC FAULTS (Series and Parallel), overload, short circuit and earth leakage. The AFDD06 is double pole RCBO AFDD meaning the Line and Neutral conductors do not have to be disconnected for IR (insulation resistance) testing if the lever is in the OFF position making it the ideal solution any property requiring AFDD protection. Arc fault protection devices (AFDD) are designed to help prevent fires by identifying fire propagating electrical arcs. These can be caused by a number of things such as rodent damage, faulty cable insulation, crushed wires or even loose terminals. These devices combine conventional analogue measurements with microprocessors to quickly analyse data. The quick ‘decision making’ of the unit allows it to detect potential faults before th…', 'Fusebox', '{"Caractéristique 1":"Available in 6A, 10A, 16A, 20A, 32A, 40A","Caractéristique 2":"Retrofit to any FuseBox Consumer Unit","Caractéristique 3":"Single module","Caractéristique 4":"Double Pole RCBO 1P+N (switched)","Caractéristique 5":"Type A for AC and pulsating DC sensitivity","Caractéristique 6":"Short circuit capacity of 6kA with a maximum rating of 40A","Caractéristique 7":"LED indication","Caractéristique 8":"Fully compliant and 3rd party tested to BS EN 62606 / IEC 61009-1"}'::jsonb, '/images/products/AFDD06faultdetectiondevice30mA.png', 'detecteurs-arc-afdd'),
  ('RTN363B-030N', 'Live Electrical 3P+N 63Amp B Curve 30mA Type A RCBO', 'live-electrical-3pn-63a-b-curve-30ma-type-a-rcbo', 'Live Electrical: This RCBO is specifically designed for Live Electrical Three Phase Distribution Boards, offering advanced protection and reliability. Combining the functions of an RCD (Residual Current Device) and an MCB (Miniature Circuit Breaker), it safeguards against overloads, short circuits, and earth leakage faults. Its Type A functionality ensures detection of both AC (Alternating Current) and pulsating DC (Direct Current) residual currents, making it ideal for modern electrical systems with sensitive equipment. Key Features of Live Electrical Three Phase RCBO 63A B Curve: Applications: Specifications:', 'Live Electrical', '{"Rated current":"63A for precise and safe load handling.","Fault current":"10kA, ensuring robust protection against high fault conditions.","RCD trip rating":"30mA to safeguard against harmful leakage currents.","Curve B":"Provides fast disconnection, suitable for residential and light commercial applications.","Type A":"Detects both AC and pulsating DC residual currents for enhanced safety.","Caractéristique 1":"Designed specifically for Live Electrical Three Phase Distribution Boards.","Caractéristique 2":"Perfect for industrial and commercial environments with modern electrical loads.","Caractéristique 3":"Ideal for systems with sensitive equipment prone to pulsating DC leakage currents.","Rated Current":"63A","Fault Current":"10kA","RCD Trip Rating":"30mA","Curve Type":"B","RCD Type":"A (AC and pulsating DC detection)","Compliance":"BS EN 61009"}'::jsonb, '/images/products/RTN50C0303PN-e1755599447487.png', 'disjoncteurs-differentiels-rcbo'),
